              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a playing field, then the Marathi for to overcome."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पदक",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पदक — padak — \"a medal\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्पर्धेत अरुणला पदक मिळालं. spardhet aruṇlā padak miḷālaṁ. Arun won a medal in the competition."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सुवर्णपदक, a gold medal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पदक (padak) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit padaka, a derivative of pada, glossed as a kind of ornament (Monier-Williams); Marathi uses it for a medal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
